
#brick

~(unlikely [tie #wire-coil to #brick])

(instead of [put $obj #in *])
	(try [tie $obj to *])

(perform [tie #wire-coil to *])
	You insert the wire coil into the brick.
	(now) (#wire-coil is #tiedto *)

(on #wire-coil timeout)
    (#brick has parent $container)
    (now) (#brick is nowhere)
    (explosion in $container)

(explosion in $container)
    ($container is in the house)
    (current room $room)
    ($room is in the house)
    The house shakes, and the ceiling of the room you're in collapses,
    turning you into a pancake.
    (jigs up)

(explosion in $container)
    { (current room $container) (or) (current player $container) }
    Now you've done it.  It seems that the brick has other properties
    than weight, namely the ability to blow you to smithereens.

(explosion in #hole)
    (#hole is in room $room)
    (now) ~(#box is closed)
    (now) (#hole is nowhere)
    (narrate explosion in room $room)

(explosion in $container)
    ($container is in room #dusty-room)
    The room trembles and 50,000 pounds of rock fall on you, turning you
    into a pancake.
    (jigs up)

(narrate explosion in room $room)
    (current room $here)
    (from $here go $ to $room)
    There is an explosion nearby.

%%%

%% SAFE
#dusty-room
(room *)
(name *)	Dusty Room
(look *)
	You are in a dusty old room which is virtually featureless, except
	for an exit on the north side.
	(par)
	(if) (#box is closed) (then)
		Imbedded in the far wall, there is a rusty old box.  It appears that
		the box is somewhat damaged, since an oblong hole has been chipped
		out of the front of it.
		(list contents of #hole)
	(else)
		On the far wall is a rusty box, whose door has been blown off.
		(list contents of #box)
	(endif)
%% TODO: room action routine SAFE-ROOM
(from * go #north to #wide-ledge)

%% FUSE
#wire-coil
(* is #in #stream)
(name *)	wire coil
(item *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	shiny thin fuse
(* size is 1)
(appearance *)
	There is a coil of thin shiny wire here.
